[Term]
id: CCTO:000022 
name: Quality of life 
def: "The subjective measurement of an individual's sense of well-being and ability to enjoy life. The concept holds varying meanings for different people and may evolve over time. For some individuals it implies autonomy, empowerment, capability, and choice; for others, security, social integration, or freedom from stress or illness." [NCIT:C17047] 
comment: QLQ C30; EORTC QLQ-C30 
synonym: "Life quality" [] 
synonym: "Patient quality of life" [] 
synonym: "QOL" EXACT [NCIT:C17047] 
synonym: "Quality of life measures" [] 
synonym: "Quality-of-Life" EXACT [NCIT:C17047] 
xref: UMLS:C0518214
