[Term]
id: CCTO:000030 
name: Efficacy 
def: "The probability of benefit to individuals in a defined population from a medical technology applied for a given medical problem under ideal conditions of use. Efficacy is a measure of effect of therapy among appropriate patients in whom treatment is tolerated and effectively administered, under the condition of sufficient patients' compliance, usually determined in randomized trials." [NCIT:C39547] 
synonym: "Clinical efficacy" [] 
synonym: "Clinical outcomes" [] 
synonym: "Treatment efficacy" EXACT [NCIT:C39547] 
xref: UMLS:C0087113
