[Term]
id: CCTO:000355 
name: Bone marrow hypocellular 
def: "A laboratory finding indicating decreased number of hematopoietic cells in the bone marrow. It may result from decreased proliferation of all or part of the hematopoietic series (erythroid, myeloid, and megakaryocytic). Microscopically, the hematopoietic cells are replaced by adipocytes OR A disorder characterized by the inability of the bone marrow to produce hematopoietic elements." [NCIT:C35167, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Bone marrow hypoplasia" EXACT [NCIT:C35167] 
synonym: "Hypocellular bone marrow" EXACT [NCIT:C35167] 
