[Term]
id: CCTO:000357 
name: Febrile neutropenia 
def: "Neutropenia associated with fever, the latter indicating the presence of an infection OR A disorder characterized by an ANC <1000/mm3 and a single temperature of >38.3 degrees C (101 degrees F) or a sustained temperature of >=38 degrees C (100.4 degrees F) for more than one hour" [NCIT:C35665, NCI:CTCAE] 
