[Term]
id: CCTO:000367 
name: Atrial fibrillation 
def: "A disorder characterized by a dysrhythmia without discernible P waves and an irregular ventricular response due to multiple reentry circuits. The rhythm disturbance originates above the ventricles OR An electrocardiographic finding of a supraventricular arrhythmia characterized by the replacement of consistent P waves by rapid oscillations or fibrillatory waves that vary in size, shape and timing and are accompanied by an irregularly irregular ventricular response. (CDISC) OR A disorder characterized by an electrocardiographic finding of a supraventricular arrhythmia characterized by the replacement of consistent P waves by rapid oscillations or fibrillatory waves that vary in size, shape and timing and are accompanied by an irregular ventricular response. (CDISC)" [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C111092, NCIT:C50466] 
synonym: "AF" EXACT [NCIT:C111092] 
synonym: "AF" EXACT [NCIT:C50466] 
