[Term]
id: CCTO:000369 
name: Atrioventricular block complete 
def: "A disorder characterized by a dysrhythmia with complete failure of atrial electrical impulse conduction through the AV node to the ventricles OR A disorder characterized by an electrocardiographic finding of complete failure of atrial electrical impulse conduction to the ventricles. This is manifested on the ECG by disassociation of atrial and ventricular rhythms. The atrial rate must be faster than the ventricular rate. (CDISC)" [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C50501] 
synonym: "AV Block Third Degree" EXACT [NCIT:C50501] 
synonym: "Atrioventricular block, third degree" EXACT [NCIT:C50501] 
