[Term]
id: CCTO:000370 
name: Atrioventricular block first degree 
def: "A disorder characterized by a dysrhythmia with a delay in the time required for the conduction of an electrical impulse through the atrioventricular (AV) node beyond 0.2 seconds; prolongation of the PR interval greater than 200 milliseconds OR A disorder characterized by an electrocardiographic finding of prolonged PR interval for a specific population. For adults one common threshold is a PR interval greater than 0.20 seconds." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C62015] 
synonym: "AV Block First Degree" EXACT [NCIT:C62015] 
synonym: "Atrioventricular block, first degree" EXACT [NCIT:C62015] 
synonym: "First Degree AV Block" EXACT [NCIT:C62015] 
synonym: "First degree atrioventricular block" EXACT [NCIT:C62015] 
