[Term]
id: CCTO:000373 
name: Constrictive pericarditis 
def: "A disorder characterized by a thickened and fibrotic pericardial sac; these fibrotic changes impede normal myocardial function by restricting myocardial muscle action OR A heart disorder in which the pericardial sac becomes thickened and fibrotic, tightening the myocardium and impeding the normal myocardial function." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C78246] 
