[Term]
id: CCTO:000382 
name: Paroxysmal atrial tachycardia 
def: "A disorder characterized by a dysrhythmia with abrupt onset and sudden termination of atrial contractions with a rate of 150-250 beats per minute. The rhythm disturbance originates in the atria OR A disorder characterized by an electrocardiographic finding of episodic atrial tachycardia with abrupt onset and termination." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C34900] 
synonym: "PAT" EXACT [NCIT:C34900] 
synonym: "True paroxysmal atrial tachycardia" EXACT [NCIT:C34900] 
