[Term]
id: CCTO:000384 
name: Pericardial tamponade 
def: "A disorder characterized by an increase in intrapericardial pressure due to the collection of blood or fluid in the pericardium OR Acute compression of the heart caused by increased intrapericardial pressure due to the collection of blood or fluid in the pericardium from rupture of the heart, penetrating trauma, or progressive effusion." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C50481] 
synonym: "Cardiac tamponade" EXACT [NCIT:C50481] 
