[Term]
id: CCTO:000389 
name: Sick sinus syndrome 
def: "A disorder characterized by a dysrhythmia with alternating periods of bradycardia and atrial tachycardia accompanied by syncope, fatigue and dizziness OR A constellation of signs and symptoms which may include syncope, fatigue, dizziness, and alternating periods of bradycardia and atrial tachycardia, which is caused by sinoatrial node dysfunction." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C62244] 
synonym: "SSS" EXACT [NCIT:C62244] 
synonym: "Sick sinus syndrome adverse event" EXACT [NCIT:C54938] 
