[Term]
id: CCTO:000390 
name: Sinus bradycardia 
def: "A disorder characterized by an electrocardiographic finding of abnormally slow heart rate with its origin in the sinus node. Thresholds for different age, gender, and patient populations exist. (CDISC) OR An electrocardiographic finding of abnormally slow heart rate with its origin in the sinus node. Thresholds for different age, gender, and patient populations exist. (CDISC) OR A disorder characterized by a dysrhythmia with a heart rate less than 60 beats per minute that originates in the sinus node." [NCIT:C26923, NCIT:C111097, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Sinus bradycardia adverse event" EXACT [NCIT:C54940] 
synonym: "Sinus Bradycardia by ECG Finding" EXACT [NCIT:C111097] 
synonym: "Sinus Bradycardia by EKG Finding" EXACT [NCIT:C111097] 
