[Term]
id: CCTO:000391 
name: Sinus tachycardia 
def: "A disorder characterized by a dysrhythmia with a heart rate greater than 100 beats per minute that originates in the sinus node OR A disorder characterized by an electrocardiographic finding of abnormally rapid heart rate with its origin in the sinus node. Thresholds for different age, gender, and patient populations exist. (CDISC) OR An electrocardiographic finding of abnormally rapid heart rate with its origin in the sinus node. Thresholds for different age, gender, and patient populations exist. (CDISC)" [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C26889, NCIT:C111104] 
synonym: "Sinus tachycardia adverse event" EXACT [NCIT:C54941] 
