[Term]
id: CCTO:000395 
name: Ventricular fibrillation 
def: "A disorder characterized by an electrocardiographic finding of a rapid grossly irregular ventricular rhythm with marked variability in QRS cycle length, morphology, and amplitude. The rate is typically greater than 300 bpm. (CDISC) OR A disorder characterized by a dysrhythmia without discernible QRS complexes due to rapid repetitive excitation of myocardial fibers without coordinated contraction of the ventricles OR An electrocardiographic finding of a rapid grossly irregular ventricular rhythm with marked variability in QRS cycle length, morphology, and amplitude. The rate is typically greater than 300 bpm. (CDISC)" [NCIT:C50799, NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C111102] 
synonym: "Fibrillation, ventricular" EXACT [NCIT:C50799] 
synonym: "VF" EXACT [NCIT:C111102] 
