[Term]
id: CCTO:000405 
name: Vestibular disorder 
def: "A disorder characterized by dizziness, imbalance, nausea, and vision problems OR A non-neoplastic or neoplastic disorder affecting the inner ear. Causes are inner ear infections, head injuries, and neoplasms (e.g., acoustic schwannoma). Symptoms include dizziness, imbalance, nausea, and vision problems." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C27166] 
