[Term]
id: CCTO:000407 
name: Cushingoid 
def: "A constellation of signs and symptoms caused by an excess of glucocorticoids. Classic features include moon facies, buffalo hump, obesity, striae and adiposity OR A disorder characterized by signs and symptoms that resemble Cushing's disease or syndrome: buffalo hump obesity, striations, adiposity, hypertension, diabetes, and osteoporosis, usually due to exogenous corticosteroids." [NCIT:C37938, NCI:CTCAE] 
