[Term]
id: CCTO:000411 
name: Hyperthyroidism 
def: "Overactivity of the thyroid gland resulting in overproduction of thyroid hormone and increased metabolic rate. Causes include diffuse hyperplasia of the thyroid gland (Graves' disease), single nodule in the thyroid gland, and thyroiditis. The symptoms are related to the increased metabolic rate and include weight loss, fatigue, heat intolerance, excessive sweating, diarrhea, tachycardia, insomnia, muscle weakness, and tremor OR A disorder characterized by excessive levels of thyroid hormone in the body. Common causes include an overactive thyroid gland or thyroid hormone overdose." [NCIT:C3123, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Overactive thyroid" EXACT [NCIT:C3123] 
xref: UMLS:C0020550
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10020850 
xref: NCIT:C3123 
