[Term]
id: CCTO:000412 
name: Hypoparathyroidism 
def: "An endocrine disorder characterized by decreased production of parathyroid hormone by the parathyroid glands. It is usually caused by damage of the parathyroid glands during head and neck surgery. Signs and symptoms include muscle cramps, abdominal pain, dry skin, brittle nails, cataracts, tetany, and convulsions OR A disorder characterized by a decrease in production of parathyroid hormone by the parathyroid glands." [NCIT:C78350, NCI:CTCAE] 
