[Term]
id: CCTO:000432 
name: Retinal detachment 
def: "A disorder characterized by the separation of the inner retina layers from the underlying pigment epithelium OR An eye emergency condition which may lead to blindness if left untreated. It is characterized by the separation of the inner retina layers from the underlying pigment epithelium. Causes include trauma, advanced diabetes mellitus, high myopia, and choroid tumors. Symptoms include sudden appearance of floaters, sudden light flushes, and blurred vision." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C26874] 
synonym: "Detached retina" EXACT [NCIT:C26874] 
synonym: "Retina, detached" EXACT [NCIT:C26874] 
synonym: "Retinal detachment adverse event" EXACT [NCIT:C55886] 
xref: UMLS:C0035305
