[Term]
id: CCTO:000433 
name: Retinal tear 
def: "A disorder characterized by a small laceration of the retina, this occurs when the vitreous separates from the retina. Symptoms include flashes and floaters OR A usually small tearing of the retina occurring when the vitreous separates from the retina. It may lead to retinal detachment. Symptoms include flashes and floaters." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C50732] 
synonym: "Retina, Tear(s) In" EXACT [NCIT:C50732] 
synonym: "Retinal tears" EXACT [NCIT:C50732] 
