[Term]
id: CCTO:000438 
name: Vitreous hemorrhage 
def: "Blood extravasation in the vitreous humor. Causes include neovascularization, retinal tear, retinal detachment, and rupture of a blood vessel aneurysm in the eye OR A disorder characterized by blood extravasation into the vitreous humor." [NCIT:C50469, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Blood in vitreous fluid" EXACT [NCIT:C50469] 
synonym: "Fluid, blood in vitreous" EXACT [NCIT:C50469] 
