[Term]
id: CCTO:000439 
name: Watering eyes 
def: "Tearing eyes; a condition caused either by tear overproduction or impaired drainage of the tear duct. Causes of tear overproduction include eye irritation (e.g., eye infection, foreign body in the eye), headache, pain reaction, allergies, sinusitis, and injury to the eye OR A disorder of excessive tearing in the eyes; it can be caused by overproduction of tears or impaired drainage of the tear duct." [NCIT:C78717, NCI:CTCAE] 
