[Term]
id: CCTO:000493 
name: Gastroesophageal reflux disease 
def: "A disorder characterized by reflux of the gastric and/or duodenal contents into the distal esophagus. It is chronic in nature and usually caused by incompetence of the lower esophageal sphincter, and may result in injury to the esophageal mucosal. Symptoms include heartburn and acid indigestion OR A chronic disorder characterized by reflux of the gastric and/or duodenal contents into the distal esophagus. It is usually caused by incompetence of the lower esophageal sphincter. Symptoms include heartburn and acid indigestion. It may cause injury to the esophageal mucosa." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C26781] 
synonym: "GERD" EXACT [NCIT:C26781] 
xref: UMLS:C0017168
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10066874 
xref: NCIT:C26781 
