[Term]
id: CCTO:000562 
name: Flu like symptoms 
def: "A disorder characterized by a group of symptoms similar to those observed in patients with the flu. It includes fever, chills, body aches, malaise, loss of appetite and dry cough OR Complaints describing a pattern similar to influenza, and may include fever, chills, muscle or body aches, cough, sore throat, rhinitis or fatigue." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C78302] 
synonym: "Flu-like symptoms" EXACT [NCIT:C78302] 
synonym: "Influenza-like illness" EXACT [NCIT:C78302] 
