[Term]
id: CCTO:000566 
name: Infusion site extravasation 
def: "A disorder characterized by leakage of a pharmacologic or a biologic substance from the infusion site into the surrounding tissue. Signs and symptoms include induration, erythema, swelling, burning sensation and marked discomfort at the infusion site OR Leakage of a pharmacologic or a biological substance from the infusion site into the surrounding tissue. Signs and symptoms include induration, erythema, swelling, burning sensation, and pain at the infusion site." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C78362] 
xref: UMLS:C1608954
