[Term]
id: CCTO:000587 
name: Portal hypertension 
def: "Increased blood pressure in the portal venous system. It is most commonly caused by cirrhosis. Other causes include portal vein thrombosis, Budd-Chiari syndrome, and right heart failure. Complications include ascites, esophageal varices, encephalopathy, and splenomegaly OR A disorder characterized by an increase in blood pressure in the portal venous system." [NCIT:C3119, NCI:CTCAE] 
