[Term]
id: CCTO:000589 
name: Allergic reaction 
def: "An immune response that occurs following re-exposure to an innocuous antigen, and that requires the presence of existing antibodies against that antigen. This response involves the binding of IgE to mast cells, and may worsen with repeated exposures OR A disorder characterized by an adverse local or general response from exposure to an allergen OR An immune response that occurs following exposure to an innocuous antigen, but that does not require the presence of preformed antibodies to the antigen." [NCIT:C114476, NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C3114] 
synonym: "Allergy" EXACT [NCIT:C114476] 
synonym: "Hypersensitive" EXACT [NCIT:C3114] 
synonym: "Hypersensitivity reaction" EXACT [NCIT:C3114] 
synonym: "Hypersensitivity" EXACT [NCIT:C3114] 
synonym: "Sensitive" EXACT [NCIT:C3114] 
synonym: "Sensitivity" EXACT [NCIT:C3114] 
synonym: "allergic response" EXACT [NCIT:C114476] 
