[Term]
id: CCTO:000592 
name: Cytokine release syndrome 
def: "A syndrome that occurs after therapeutic infusion of antibodies into the blood and is characterized by nausea, headache, tachycardia, hypotension, rash, and shortness of breath. It is caused by the release of cytokines from the cells that are targeted by the antibodies. Most patients experience a mild to moderate reaction; however, the reaction may be severe and life-threatening OR A disorder characterized by nausea, headache, tachycardia, hypotension, rash, and shortness of breath; it is caused by the release of cytokines from the cells." [NCIT:C78251, NCI:CTCAE] 
xref: UMLS:C0948245
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10052015 
xref: NCIT:C78251 
