[Term]
id: CCTO:000597 
name: Appendicitis perforated 
def: "Acute appendicitis with gangrenous changes resulting in the rupture of the appendiceal wall. The appendiceal wall rupture causes the release of inflammatory and bacterial contents from the appendiceal lumen into the abdominal cavity OR A disorder characterized by acute inflammation to the vermiform appendix caused by a pathogenic agent with gangrenous changes resulting in the rupture of the appendiceal wall. The appendiceal wall rupture causes the release of inflammatory and bacterial contents from the appendiceal lumen into the abdominal cavity." [NCIT:C78178, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Acute perforated appendicitis" EXACT [NCIT:C78178] 
xref: UMLS:C0564755
xref: UMLS:C0854119
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10003012 
