[Term]
id: CCTO:000618 
name: Eye infection 
def: "An infectious process affecting any part of the eye. Causes include viruses and bacteria. Symptoms include itching and discomfort in the eye, watery eyes, eye pain and discharge, and blurring vision. Representative examples include pink eye, blepharitis, and trachoma OR A disorder characterized by an infectious process involving the eye." [NCIT:C45372, NCI:CTCAE] 
