[Term]
id: CCTO:000623 
name: Infective myositis 
def: "A disorder characterized by an infectious process involving the skeletal muscles OR An infectious process affecting the skeletal muscles. It can be caused by viruses (including HIV), bacteria, fungi, and parasites. Symptoms include muscle weakness and muscle pain." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C26984] 
synonym: "Infectious myositis" EXACT [NCIT:C26984] 
