[Term]
id: CCTO:000626 
name: Laryngitis 
def: "An acute or chronic, bacterial or viral inflammatory process affecting the larynx. Signs and symptoms include sore throat, cough, swallowing difficulties, and hoarseness OR A disorder characterized by an inflammatory process involving the larynx OR An acute inflammatory process affecting the larynx.  It is caused by bacteria, viruses, or vocal strain.  Signs and symptoms include sore throat, cough, swallowing difficulties, and hoarseness." [NCIT:C26811, NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C26688] 
synonym: "Acute laryngitis" EXACT [NCIT:C26688] 
synonym: "Laryngeal inflammation" EXACT [NCIT:C26811] 
