[Term]
id: CCTO:000636 
name: Papulopustular rash 
def: "Skin eruption consisting of papules and pustules, most often appearing in the face, scalp, and upper trunk.  It is usually caused by corticosteroids or epidermal growth factor receptor inhibitors OR A disorder characterized by an eruption consisting of papules (a small, raised pimple) and pustules (a small pus filled blister), typically appearing in face, scalp, and upper chest and back Unlike acne, this rash does not present with whiteheads or blackheads, and can be symptomatic, with itchy or tender lesions." [NCIT:C80119, NCI:CTCAE] 
xref: UMLS:C2609319
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10069138 
xref: NCIT:C80119 
