[Term]
id: CCTO:000637 
name: Paronychia 
def: "An acute or chronic infection of the soft tissues around the nail. Symptoms include pain, tenderness, erythema, and swelling around the nail. Acute infection results from minor trauma to the fingertip and Staphylococcus aureus is usually the causative agent. Chronic infection is usually caused by Candida albicans OR A disorder characterized by an infectious process involving the soft tissues around the nail." [NCIT:C79702, NCI:CTCAE] 
xref: UMLS:C0030578
xref: UMLS:C1075202
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10034016 
