[Term]
id: CCTO:000655 
name: Soft tissue infection 
def: "A bacterial infectious process affecting the soft tissues. A severe form caused by anaerobic or aerobic bacteria is associated with soft tissues necrosis and affects the subcutaneous adipose tissue, muscles, fascia, and the skin OR A disorder characterized by an infectious process involving soft tissues." [NCIT:C79745, NCI:CTCAE] 
