[Term]
id: CCTO:000656 
name: Splenic infection 
def: "An infectious process affecting the spleen. Predisposing factors include immunosuppression, diabetes mellitus, and sickle cell anemia. Infectious agents include bacteria (e.g., staphylococcus and streptococcus) and fungi OR A disorder characterized by an infectious process involving the spleen." [NCIT:C78627, NCI:CTCAE] 
