[Term]
id: CCTO:000660 
name: Upper respiratory infection 
def: "A disorder characterized by an infectious process involving the upper respiratory tract (nose, paranasal sinuses, pharynx, larynx, or trachea) OR An infectious process affecting the upper respiratory tract (nose, paranasal sinuses, pharynx, larynx, or trachea). Symptoms include congestion, sneezing, coughing, fever, and sore throat." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C35650] 
synonym: "Cold" EXACT [NCIT:C35650] 
synonym: "Infection, upper respiratory tract" EXACT [NCIT:C35650] 
synonym: "Upper respiratory tract infection" EXACT [NCIT:C35650] 
synonym: "Upper respiratory tract inflammation" EXACT [NCIT:C35650] 
