[Term]
id: CCTO:000662 
name: Urinary tract infection 
def: "A disorder characterized by an infectious process involving the urinary tract, most commonly the bladder and the urethra OR A bacterial infectious process affecting any part of the urinary tract, most commonly the bladder and the urethra. Symptoms include urinary urgency and frequency, burning sensation during urination, lower abdominal discomfort, and cloudy urine." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C50791] 
synonym: "Infection, urinary tract" EXACT [NCIT:C50791] 
synonym: "Tract, infection of urinary" EXACT [NCIT:C50791] 
synonym: "UTI" EXACT [NCIT:C50791] 
synonym: "Urinary tract infectious disease" EXACT [NCIT:C50791] 
