[Term]
id: CCTO:000663 
name: Uterine infection 
def: "An acute or chronic, usually bacterial infectious process affecting the endometrium. It may extend to the myometrium and parametrial tissues. Symptoms include lower abdominal pain, vaginal discharge, and vaginal bleeding OR A disorder characterized by an infectious process involving the endometrium. It may extend to the myometrium and parametrial tissues." [NCIT:C26764, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Endometritis" EXACT [NCIT:C26764] 
