[Term]
id: CCTO:000667 
name: Ankle fracture 
def: "Traumatic or pathological injury to the ankle joint in which the continuity of an ankle bone is broken. Symptoms include pain, swelling, and difficulty moving the affected leg and foot OR A finding of damage to the ankle joint characterized by a break in the continuity of the ankle bone. Symptoms include marked discomfort, swelling and difficulty moving the affected leg and foot." [NCIT:C26989, NCI:CTCAE] 
