[Term]
id: CCTO:000673 
name: Burn 
def: "A traumatic injury involving interruption of tissue cohesiveness that results from exposure to caustic chemicals, extreme heat, extreme cold or excessive radiation OR A finding of impaired integrity to the anatomic site of an adverse thermal reaction. Burns can be caused by exposure to chemicals, direct heat, electricity, flames and radiation. The extent of damage depends on the length and intensity of exposure and time until provision of treatment." [NCIT:C34441, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Burn adverse event" EXACT [NCIT:C57900] 
synonym: "Burn of device or device component" EXACT [NCIT:C63286] 
synonym: "Burn(s)" EXACT [NCIT:C34441] 
