[Term]
id: CCTO:000780 
name: Acidosis 
def: "An abnormally high acidity of the blood and other body tissues. Acidosis can be either respiratory or metabolic OR A disorder characterized by abnormally high acidity (high hydrogen-ion concentration) of the blood and other body tissues OR Increased acidity in the blood secondary to acid base imbalance. Causes include diabetes, kidney failure and shock OR An abnormally high acidity (excess hydrogen-ion concentration) of the blood and other body tissues." [NCIT:C83504, NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C28228, NCIT:C37906] 
synonym: "Metabolic acidosis" EXACT [NCIT:C28228] 
