[Term]
id: CCTO:000800 
name: Iron overload 
def: "An adverse event resulting in accumulation of iron in the tissues OR Accumulation of iron in the tissues. It may be a manifestation of an inherited disorder (e.g., hemochromatosis) or acquired (in patients with repeated blood transfusions). Symptoms include hepatomegaly, arthritis, diabetes mellitus, and bronzed skin. If untreated it has a progressive course and may lead to death OR A disorder characterized by accumulation of iron in the tissues." [NCIT:C55993, NCIT:C78393, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Iron overload adverse event" EXACT [NCIT:C55993] 
xref: UMLS:C0282193
xref: UMLS:C1963148
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10065973 
xref: NCIT:C55993 
xref: NCIT:C78393 
