[Term]
id: CCTO:000806 
name: Avascular necrosis 
def: "Necrotic changes in the bone tissue due to interruption of blood supply. Most often affecting the epiphysis of the long bones, the necrotic changes result in the collapse and the destruction of the bone structure OR Tissue death resulting from an interruption to the blood supply OR A disorder characterized by necrotic changes in the bone tissue due to interruption of blood supply. Most often affecting the epiphysis of the long bones, the necrotic changes result in the collapse and the destruction of the bone structure." [NCIT:C34841, NCIT:C118385, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "AVN" EXACT [NCIT:C118385] 
synonym: "Avascular Necrosis of Bone" EXACT [NCIT:C34841] 
xref: UMLS:C0027543
