[Term]
id: CCTO:000976 
name: Prostatic obstruction 
def: "A disorder characterized by compression of the urethra secondary to enlargement of the prostate gland. This results in voiding difficulties (straining to void, slow urine stream, and incomplete emptying of the bladder) OR Squeezing of the urethra secondary to enlargement of the prostate gland, resulting in voiding symptoms (straining to void, slow urine stream, and incomplete emptying of the bladder)." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C78573] 
