[Term]
id: CCTO:001001 
name: Aspiration 
def: "Procedure using suction, usually with a thin needle and syringe, to remove bodily fluid or tissue OR Accidental inhalation of a foreign material into the lungs OR A disorder characterized by inhalation of solids or liquids into the lungs OR The entry of foreign material past the trachea, and into the lower respiratory tract. Oro-pharyngeal or gastric secretions are the most commonly aspirated materials, and can cause a pneumonitis or pneumonia." [NCIT:C15631, NCIT:C83507, NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C28245] 
synonym: "Aspiration adverse event" EXACT [NCIT:C28245] 
synonym: "Respiratory tract aspiration" EXACT [NCIT:C83507] 
synonym: "Unintentional material aspiration" EXACT [NCIT:C83507] 
