[Term]
id: CCTO:001009 
name: Chylothorax 
def: "A disorder characterized by milky pleural effusion (abnormal collection of fluid) resulting from accumulation of lymph fluid in the pleural cavity OR A milky pleural effusion resulting from accumulation of lymph fluid in the pleural cavity. Causes include malignancies (usually lymphoma), trauma to the thoracic duct, tuberculosis, sarcoidosis, and congenital causes OR Chylothorax resulting from a known treatment." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C79546, NCIT:C58027] 
synonym: "Chylothorax adverse event" EXACT [NCIT:C58027] 
