[Term]
id: CCTO:001013 
name: Hiccups 
def: "A disorder characterized by repeated gulp sounds that result from an involuntary opening and closing of the glottis. This is attributed to a spasm of the diaphragm OR An involuntary contraction of the diaphragm against closed vocal cords, producing the ''hic'' sound." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C37966] 
