[Term]
id: CCTO:001015 
name: Hypoxia 
def: "A decrease in the amount of oxygen in the body. Symptoms range from mild (impaired judgment, memory loss, impaired motor coordination) to severe (seizures and coma) OR A disorder characterized by a decrease in the level of oxygen in the body." [NCIT:C3890, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Hypoxia adverse event" EXACT [NCIT:C58188] 
synonym: "Hypoxic" EXACT [NCIT:C3890] 
