[Term]
id: CCTO:001023 
name: Laryngospasm 
def: "Paroxysmal spasmodic muscular contraction of the vocal cords. It is brief, usually lasting for less than one minute, interrupting the speech and breathing and may produce a high-pitched breathing sound. It may occur under anesthesia or may be associated with gastroesophageal reflex disease OR A disorder characterized by paroxysmal spasmodic muscular contraction of the vocal cords." [NCIT:C79609, NCI:CTCAE] 
xref: UMLS:C0023066
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10023891 
