[Term]
id: CCTO:001040 
name: Pulmonary fibrosis 
def: "Chronic progressive interstitial lung disorder characterized by the replacement of the lung tissue by connective tissue, leading to progressive dyspnea, respiratory failure, or right heart failure. Causes include chronic inflammatory processes, exposure to environmental irritants, radiation therapy, autoimmune disorders, certain drugs, or it may be idiopathic (no identifiable cause) OR A disorder characterized by the replacement of the lung tissue by connective tissue, leading to progressive dyspnea, respiratory failure or right heart failure." [NCIT:C26869, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Pulmonary interstitial fibrosis" EXACT [NCIT:C26869] 
xref: UMLS:C0034069
xref: UMLS:C0240035
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10037383 
xref: NCIT:C26869 
