[Term]
id: CCTO:001046 
name: Sleep apnea 
def: "Cessation of breathing for short periods during sleep. It is classified as obstructive, central, or mixed obstructive-central. It can occur at any age but it is more frequent in people over forty. Risk factors include male sex and obesity OR A disorder characterized by cessation of breathing for short periods during sleep." [NCIT:C26884, NCI:CTCAE] 
