[Term]
id: CCTO:001052 
name: Voice alteration 
def: "A disorder characterized by a change in the sound and/or speed of the voice OR Change in the sound and/or speed of the voice. Causes include laryngeal polyp, laryngitis, laryngeal carcinoma, throat carcinoma, Parkinson's disease, multiple sclerosis, stroke, hypothyroidism, oral surgery, tracheostomy, tracheal injury, and laryngeal injury." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C61043] 
