[Term]
id: CCTO:001054 
name: Alopecia 
def: "Hair loss usually from the scalp. It may result in bald spots or spread to the entire scalp or the entire epidermis. It may be androgenetic or caused by chemotherapeutic agents, compulsive hair pulling, autoimmune disorders or congenital conditions OR Hair loss usually from the scalp. It may result in bald spots or spread to the entire scalp or the entire epidermis. It may be androgenetic or caused by chemotherapeutic agents, compulsive hair pulling, autoimmune disorders, and congenital conditions OR A disorder characterized by a decrease in density of hair compared to normal for a given individual at a given age and body location." [NCIT:C50575, NCIT:C2865, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Alopecia areata" EXACT [NCIT:C50575] 
synonym: "Hair loss" EXACT [NCIT:C50575] 
synonym: "Loss of hair" EXACT [NCIT:C50575] 
