[Term]
id: CCTO:001058 
name: Erythema multiforme 
def: "A hypersensitivity reaction characterized by the sudden appearance of symmetrical cutaneous and mucocutaneous macular or papular lesions which evolve into lesions with bright red borders (target lesions). The lesions usually appear in the hands, feet, extremities, and face. Symptoms include fever, malaise, sore throat, cough, vomiting, diarrhea, arthralgia, and myalgia. Causes include infections (most commonly herpes simplex virus), drugs (e.g., sulfonamides, anticonvulsants, and antibiotics), malignancies, and collagen vascular disorders OR A disorder characterized by target lesions (a pink-red ring around a pale center)." [NCIT:C3024, NCI:CTCAE] 
xref: UMLS:C0014742
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10015218 
xref: NCIT:C3024 
