[Term]
id: CCTO:001076 
name: Rash maculo-papular 
def: "A skin condition consisting of both macules and papules OR A disorder characterized by the presence of macules (flat) and papules (elevated). Also known as morbillform rash, it is one of the most common cutaneous adverse events, frequently affecting the upper trunk, spreading centripetally and associated with pruritis." [NCIT:C75579, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Maculopapular lesion" EXACT [NCIT:C75579] 
xref: UMLS:C0423791
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10037868 
