[Term]
id: CCTO:001086 
name: Capillary leak syndrome 
def: "A disorder characterized by leakage of intravascular fluids into the extravascular space. This syndrome is observed in patients who demonstrate a state of generalized leaky capillaries following shock syndromes, low-flow states, ischemia-reperfusion injuries, toxemias, medications, or poisoning.  It can lead to generalized edema and multiple organ failure OR A syndrome characterized by leakage of intravascular fluids into the extravascular space. This syndrome is observed in patients who demonstrate a state of generalized leaky capillaries following shock syndromes, low-flow states, ischemia-reperfusion injuries, toxemias, medications, or poisoning. It can lead to generalized edema and multiple organ failure." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C62578] 
synonym: "AVLS" EXACT [NCIT:C62578] 
synonym: "Acute vascular leak syndrome" EXACT [NCIT:C62578] 
synonym: "CLS" EXACT [NCIT:C62578] 
