[Term]
id: CCTO:001097 
name: Superficial thrombophlebitis 
def: "A disorder characterized by a blood clot and inflammation involving a superficial vein of the extremities OR Thrombosis and inflammation of a superficial vein of the extremities. Symptoms include red discoloration and warmth of the skin and pain along the affected vein." [NCI:CTCAE, NCIT:C78634] 
xref: UMLS:C1510431
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10042554 
xref: NCIT:C78634 
