[Term]
id: CCTO:001100 
name: Vasculitis 
def: "An inflammatory process involving the wall of the vessels (large, medium, or small-sized vessels). The inflammatory process may cause necrosis or formation of granulomas in the vascular wall. It may be the result of an autoimmune disorder, infection, or malignancy. Representative examples include polyarteritis nodosa, temporal arteritis, Wegener granulomatosis, Kawasaki disease, Takayasu arteritis, and Henoch-Schonlein purpura OR A disorder characterized by inflammation involving the wall of a vessel." [NCIT:C26912, NCI:CTCAE] 
synonym: "Vasculitis adverse event" EXACT [NCIT:C54741] 
xref: UMLS:C0042384
xref: UMLS:C1963274
xref: NCI:CTCAE:10047115 
xref: NCIT:C26912 
xref: NCIT:C54741 
